                                SpeedPass v1.1

                              Idea by: Rille/SCX
                         v1.1 ideas by: Rille/SCX & Me

«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»

                                Important note!
                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use
it, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever
this door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but
you never know what those lamers do!).

«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»

                                   History!
                                  ~~~~~~~~~~
v1.0 - First release. Let you set a NUP's for any connectspeeds. Supports
       diffrent NUP's for all connect speeds, and unlimited speeds/pw's.
v1.1 - The door didn't allways drop carrier if the user didn't know the
       password. This is strange, since it does allways do it when I try it,
       but now this is fixed, hopefully! The door will not hang up if run on a
       local node though, however it will drop carrier on callers! I also added
       some stars, so the user wont see what he's typing!

«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»

                                 Installation!
                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If you run /X 3.x, copy all files I've supplied and you're almost set.

If you run /X 2.x or S-Express, insert the followin line to your
"commands/sys.cmd" file.

---( cut )---
SPEEDPW   XM001DOORS:SpeedPass/SpeedPass.x
---( cut )---

The first thing you have to do is to edit the SpeedPass.x.info icon. There are
one special keyword wich you can use.

ATTEMPTS=3

This let the user guess 3 times at the pw before he's kicked. Besides this you
may put any baudrate in the icon.

2400=PassWord

This sets the 2400 password to "PassWord". The passwords are NOT case
sensetive. You may add as many of these as you want.

The last thing to do is to put the following in fex your "GuestLogon.txt" in
order to have the door run at every newuser logon.

---( cut )---
~
~CC_SPEEDPW|
---( cut )---

